            <ArticleTitle>The Duke experience with nucleus caudalis DREZ coagulation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>111-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The results of 46 nucleus caudalis DREZ coagulations performed at Duke in the preceding 5 years are reviewed retrospectively, with a mean follow-up of 32 months. Fifteen (38%) of 39 patients with complete data indicated that they would undergo the procedure again. Fifteen (38%) described improved quality of life. Outcome was fair or better in 18 (46%). Complications in the form of ataxia were present in 21 (54%).</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
